findings.description:
The diff removes a security test that asserts `_.template` throws when the `variable` option contains characters that allow breaking out of the `with (obj)` block (e.g., `){malicious_code} with(obj`). The removed code in `lodash.js` also deletes the guard `reForbiddenIdentifierChars.test(variable)` which was responsible for rejecting such inputs. While the PR description says this is to prevent command injection, the diff actually *reverts* the fix from #5085, reintroducing the vulnerability. In `lodash.js`, the `_.template` function now accepts *any* string as `variable` and interpolates it directly into the generated source: `source = 'with (' + variable + ') {
' + source + '
}
'`. An attacker who controls the `variable` option can inject arbitrary code, e.g., `variable = '); require("child_process").execSync("rm -rf /"); with(obj'`.
